C++23 implements the compiler itself.

Paracine source is compiled directly into native instructions.

LLVM, an external assembler, an external compiler and an external executable linker are not dependencies of the canonical compilation path.

## 1.3 Edition separation

Edition 2026 remains a stable semantic compatibility profile.

Edition 2027 extends the language through explicit edition-aware rules, preserving established program behavior.

The compiler maintains independent grammar and semantic profiles for each edition.

A 2026 program compiled under the 2026 profile retains its original rules for syntax, arithmetic, ownership, control flow, closures, effects and failure behavior.

A source file or package compiled under the 2027 profile receives the additional capabilities defined in this standard.

Internal compiler improvements that preserve all observable semantics apply across compatible editions.

Language changes that alter observable behavior require explicit edition selection.

## 1.4 Native target classification

The production target registry distinguishes four concepts:

| Classification | Definition |
|---|---|
| Canonical | The primary reference realization of the language |
| Qualified | A target satisfying its published conformance profile |
| Specialized | A target with documented additional or restricted facilities |
| Interoperability | An output or adapter that does not replace native compilation |

Windows x86-64 with Microsoft x64 ABI, COFF and PE32+ is the canonical production configuration.

ELF, Mach-O and additional ABIs operate under their own target contracts.

Target availability never changes the meaning of target-independent source semantics.

