## 8.3 PE32+ image structure

The linker emits conventional executable sections:

```text
.text
.rdata
.data
.pdata
.xdata
.idata
.edata
.reloc
.tls
.rsrc
.debug
```

File alignment is 512 bytes.

Section alignment is 4096 bytes.

The default executable image base is `0x0000000140000000`.

Executable memory permissions honor W^X principles.

## 8.4 Native security settings

Production images use:

- Dynamic-base relocatability.
- High-entropy virtual addresses.
- NX compatibility.
- Compatible terminal-server awareness.
- Correct stack alignment.
- Valid unwind records.
- Protected image sections.
- Resource-bounded linker parsing.

Control Flow Guard is enabled when the complete required metadata is present.

A requested but unsupported CFG configuration is rejected rather than silently weakened.

## 8.5 Debug information

The Windows debugging architecture supports CodeView and PDB information.

Debug data carries source locations, routines, variables, types, scopes, parameters and native realization mappings.

Linux DWARF and other platform-specific debug formats follow their respective target profiles.

