# APPENDIX B — CANONICAL ENGINEERING EXAMPLES

## B.1 Ownership-preserving computation

```pcn
routine accumulate(values: view<int>) gives int
    var total: int = 0

    for value in values
        total += value

    give total
```

## B.2 Inclusive directed loop

```pcn
from index = 10 to 0
    process(index)
```

## B.3 Guarded iteration

```pcn
for value in values while value < threshold
    process(value)
```

## B.4 Post-test repetition

```pcn
continue until completed
    advance()
```

## B.5 Concrete closure

```pcn
routine scaled_total(
    values: view<int>,
    factor: int
) gives int

    let scale =
        move routine(value: int) gives int => value * factor

    var total: int = 0

    for value in values
        total += scale(value)

    give total
```

## B.6 Reversible mutation

```pcn
checkpoint @transaction
    update_local_state()

    if validation_failed
        rollback @transaction
        fail TransactionError.invalid
```

## B.7 Knowledge reasoning trace

```text
Source:
    value < limit

SKM:
    value : int
    limit : int

Semantic Judgment:
    comparison result : bool

Structural Analysis:
    candidate boundary guard

SCM:
